Copyright (c) 2009-2021, Redis Ltd. All rights reserved.
License: BSD-3-Clause; full terms in LICENSES/Redis-script-lua.txt.

The interpreter follows Redis's protected-call behavior and read-only table
extension. Redis is also an external reference service. The original reference
corpus and capture wrapper were supplied by acneism on 2026-10-24.
New reference answers are captured from Redis with the same wrapper.

Redis 7.2.16, src/rand.c
Copyright (c) 2010-2012, Salvatore Sanfilippo <antirez at gmail dot com>
All rights reserved.
License: BSD-3-Clause; full terms in LICENSES/Redis-rand.txt.

The state-local random generator follows Redis's rand48 recurrence and seed
conversion. The Lua string, table, and math libraries adapt the upstream
implementations listed above.

No bit, struct, cjson, cmsgpack, fpconv, CRC64, or LZF implementation is included
in A2. Add notices from the exact upstream source headers when porting them.

ARM optimized-routines, release v21.02
Copyright (c) 2018-2020, Arm Limited.
License: MIT; full terms in LICENSES/ARM-optimized-routines.txt.

libmath.go and libmath_data.go adapt math/exp.c, log.c, pow.c, exp_data.c,
log_data.c, and pow_log_data.c. Immutable bit tables retain the upstream
constants. Explicit FMA and rounding follow the Redis x86-64 glibc reference.
Source: https://github.com/ARM-software/optimized-routines/tree/v21.02/math

